#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:1
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:3
msgid ""
"`nix-copy-closure` - copy store objects to or from a remote machine via SSH"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:5
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr "概要"

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:7
msgid ""
"`nix-copy-closure` \\[`--to` | `--from` \\] \\[`--gzip`\\] \\[`--include-"
"outputs`\\] \\[`--use-substitutes` | `-s`\\] \\[`-v`\\] "
"\\[_user_@\\]_machine_\\[:_port_\\] _paths_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:15
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:17
msgid ""
"Given _paths_ from one machine, `nix-copy-closure` computes the [closure](../"
"glossary.md#gloss-closure) of those paths (i.e. all their dependencies in "
"the Nix store), and copies [store objects](../glossary.md#gloss-store-"
"object) in that closure to another machine via SSH. It doesn’t copy store "
"objects that are already present on the other machine."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:20
#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:285
msgid "**Note**"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:22
msgid ""
"While the Nix store to use on the local machine can be specified on the "
"command line with the [`--store`](../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-store) "
"option, the Nix store to be accessed on the remote machine can only be "
"[configured statically](../command-ref/conf-file.md#configuration-file) on "
"that remote machine."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:24
msgid ""
"Since `nix-copy-closure` calls `ssh`, you may need to authenticate with the "
"remote machine. In fact, you may be asked for authentication _twice_ because "
"`nix-copy-closure` currently connects twice to the remote machine: first to "
"get the set of paths missing on the target machine, and second to send the "
"dump of those paths. When using public key authentication, you can avoid "
"typing the passphrase with `ssh-agent`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:28
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:30
msgid "`--to`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:32
msgid ""
"Copy the closure of _paths_ from a Nix store accessible from the local "
"machine to the Nix store on the remote _machine_. This is the default "
"behavior."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:35
msgid "`--from`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:37
msgid ""
"Copy the closure of _paths_ from the Nix store on the remote _machine_ to "
"the local machine's specified Nix store."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:39
msgid "`--gzip`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:41
msgid "Enable compression of the SSH connection."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:43
msgid "`--include-outputs`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:45
msgid ""
"Also copy the outputs of [store derivation](../glossary.md#gloss-store-"
"derivation)s included in the closure."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:49
msgid "`--use-substitutes` / `-s`"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/nix-copy-closure.md:51
msgid ""
"Attempt to download missing store objects on the target from [substituters]"
"(../command-ref/conf-file.md#conf-substituters). Any store objects that "
"cannot be substituted on the target are still copied normally from the "
"source. This is useful, for instance, if the connection between the source "
"and target machine is slow, but the connection between the target machine "
"and `cache.nixos.org` (the default binary cache server) is fast."
msgstr ""

